  "about": [
    "What the app relies on the Codex CLI doing, that a fake Codex CLI reproduces, for the minimum and pinned versions the",
    "contract names. Each entry is sourced: a sanitised real capture (P3.1, tests/fixtures/codex/cli/<version>/, see",
    "ANONYMISED.txt there), the app-server schema the CLI itself generated (tests/fixtures/codex/app-server/<version>/),",
    "or a pinned-source/doc citation (a file of this repo, the versions it speaks for, a quote it contains). Nothing",
    "here is taken from a fake. tests/wp1/fake-cli-oracle.test.ts checks every entry against its sources (the real side)",
    "and every fake against every entry it claims (the fake side)."
  ],
  "rules": {
    "lines": "A stream is split on line feeds (carriage returns dropped); blank lines are ignored.",
    "modes": "exactly: the stream has exactly these lines, in order. inOrder: these lines occur in this order, other lines may sit between them. document: the whole stream is one JSON value.",
    "streams": "either: the lines hold on stdout or on stderr (the app reads both).",
    "matchers": "exact: the line itself. regex: an anchored regular expression. rpcResult: a JSON-RPC answer with this id whose result has these fields. json: the document has these fields. {version} stands for the entry version (escaped inside a regex).",
    "exitCode": "A number, or \"nonzero\". Absent: not asserted, and a citation says why.",
    "afterwards": "Then the named entry is run in the same realm and must hold too.",
    "backing": "For each version an entry covers, its exit code, its lines, an either stream and its afterwards must each be backed by a capture or schema of that version or by a citation that says so; a citation carries the value it backs (exitCode, afterwards) and the samples its quote holds, which the entry lines must accept."
